@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.1.29
@changelog
  - Codename: Impossible to walk in this muck. No footing at all.
  - New: UF8 device tab in the Learn-HUD — interactive strip-grid (8 strips × V-Pot / Fader / Solo / Cut / Sel), bank-aware (Top-Soft-Keys pick the V-Pot bank); click a bank to switch it
  - New: UF8 Parameter List — open the drawer, type to filter, pick a parameter, click a cell to bind it (no wiggle); bound params show a green dot
  - New: UF8 Touch-to-Learn — arm a cell by moving its control on the hardware (touch a fader, turn a V-Pot, press Solo/Cut/Sel), then wiggle a plug-in parameter to bind
  - New: map an unmapped plug-in straight from the HUD (the first bind bootstraps a UF8-only map); right-click a cell for Invert / Fill sequential / Unbind / V-Pot value-toggle mode
  - New: UF8 hardware-mockup view (toggle List ↔ Mockup), faithful to the FX-Learn UF8 face; all learn / colour / bank interactions work in both views
  - New: V-Pot bank colours — right-click a bank → 10-swatch SSL palette sets its Top-Soft-Key LED colour; "Bar colour (all)" paints the active bank's display colour bars
  - New: UC1 Control+Option FX-Learn layer — a fourth modifier overlay, so one knob can carry up to four mappings
  - New: 10 knob feel-preset slots (was 5)
  - Fix: UC1 two-knob "fight for priority" — the input parser now walks every frame in a USB transfer; modifier-layer knob travel + focused readout fall back correctly
  - Fix: Esc cancels a HUD learn / assign even when the HUD isn't focused; the held modifier layer is latched at context-menu open; Esc also closes the FX-Learn curve editor popup
  - Fix: console spam gone (full ReaImGui header signature-drift audit)
